    "seoTitle": "What Should a Trade Website Include? | TradeBuilt UK Advice.",
    "metaDescription": "Make your trade website easier to use with clear service pages, genuine work photos and simple contact options. Explore the essentials with TradeBuilt’s advice.",
    "fullArticle": "<p>A good trade website helps a potential customer make a decision. It explains what you do, where you work and how to contact you, without making them hunt for the answer.</p><h2>Start with your services and areas</h2><p>A visitor should quickly understand whether you can help with their job. Be specific about your services and the areas you cover. A roofing company, for example, might explain roof repairs, replacements and flat roofing separately.</p><p>Use familiar terms your customers recognise. Describe what the service involves and the situations it is suitable for. A short, clear explanation is more useful than a long list of broad claims.</p><h2>Show evidence of your work</h2><p>Use photographs of real projects when you have permission to publish them. Explain the work completed, the problem solved and any details that show your care and experience.</p><p>Only include qualifications, accreditations and customer feedback you can substantiate. Specific evidence gives people something concrete to assess.</p><h2>Make contact straightforward</h2><p>Give visitors an obvious way to call or send an enquiry. Keep forms focused on the information you need to respond, and explain what will happen after submission.</p><p>Check the experience on your own phone. Can you read the text comfortably? Are buttons easy to tap? Is your phone number easy to find?</p><h2>Keep the basics current</h2><p>Review your contact details, services and coverage as your business changes. Remove services you no longer offer and avoid leaving outdated information where a customer could rely on it.</p><p>A website does not need to say everything. It needs to answer the important questions and make the next step clear.</p><div class=\"callout\"><p>Planning your next website? <a href=\"../pay-monthly-websites.html\">Explore TradeBuilt’s pay monthly website packages</a> or <a href=\"../contact.html\">talk through what you need</a>.</p></div>"
