    "metaDescription": "Compare pay monthly website packages with confidence. Know what to ask about design, content, support, ownership and cancellation before choosing your provider.",
    "fullArticle": "<p>Pay monthly websites spread the cost of your online presence. To compare packages properly, start with what your business needs, then look closely at what each service includes.</p><h2>Define the job your website needs to do</h2><p>Write down your core services, the areas you cover and the action you want visitors to take. A small business with one main service may need a different structure from a team offering several specialist services.</p><p>Be clear about whether you need a new logo, help with writing or support choosing photographs. These tasks should be discussed as part of the scope.</p><h2>Ask what happens after launch</h2><p>Check what website care and support mean in practice. Ask about content changes, hosting, security maintenance and how to request help.</p><p>If search optimisation is included, find out whether this means initial setup or ongoing work. Ask for the agreed activities and review process to be explained clearly.</p><h2>Understand the commercial details</h2><ul><li>Is VAT included in the displayed price?</li><li>Are there setup fees or separately charged services?</li><li>Who owns the domain, content and website?</li><li>What happens to hosting and access if you cancel?</li><li>If you pay annually, how are cancellation and refunds handled?</li></ul><p>Get the answers in writing before you commit. Clear expectations make it easier for both you and your provider to work well together.</p><h2>Choose the right fit</h2><p>The useful comparison is the overall service, not just the lowest monthly figure. Look for an approach you understand and a package that reflects your business priorities.</p><div class=\"callout\"><p><a href=\"../pay-monthly-websites.html\">See TradeBuilt’s draft package options</a> and <a href=\"../faqs.html\">read our answers to common questions</a>.</p></div>"
