    "seoTitle": "Make Your Trade Project Photos Work Harder | TradeBuilt Tips",
    "metaDescription": "Show the quality of your trade work with useful project photos & clear descriptions. Learn what to capture, explain and check before adding images to your site.",
    "fullArticle": "<p>The work you finish every week can help future customers understand your business. A useful project photograph shows more than a neat result when it is accompanied by a clear explanation.</p><h2>Capture the context and the detail</h2><p>Take a wider photograph that shows the completed job, then a few closer views of the details that matter. Keep the camera level, check the lighting and move distracting items where it is safe to do so.</p><p>Where appropriate, before and after photographs can explain the change. Try to keep the viewpoint similar so the comparison is easy to understand.</p><h2>Write down what happened</h2><p>Make a few notes while the work is fresh in your mind. What did the customer need? What did your team do? Was there a practical challenge worth explaining?</p><p>These details help turn a photograph into useful information. Avoid broad statements that could describe any job.</p><h2>Check permission and privacy</h2><p>Agree what can be shared with your customer. Review photographs for people, number plates, house numbers and other details that should not be published. Use only images you have the right to use.</p><h2>Keep everything easy to find</h2><p>Save photographs in clearly named folders and keep the project notes alongside them. A little organisation makes future website updates much easier.</p><p>Choose the images that best explain the work. A focused selection is often more helpful than a large set of nearly identical photographs.</p><div class=\"callout\"><p>Want a website that reflects the quality of your work? <a href=\"../contact.html\">Talk to TradeBuilt about your website</a>.</p></div>"
